.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::NimbleRegion< dim >"Flexible collection of \fBElement\fP and \fBNode\fP object pointers to be used by the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP, which also requires access to ranges of (perimeter) nodes\&.

.PP
\fBNimbleRegion\fP is a light (non-unique) version of \fBRegion\fP that can grow or shrink, retaining the knowledge of its perimeter\&.

.PP
Like \fBRegion\fP, \fBNimbleRegion\fP keeps track of its perimeter, which always includes a halo that comes about as all elements that contain user-supplied nodes (and additional ones) will be included into the contructed region\&.

.PP
The region is based on the STL vector and operated under a high-memory policy\&. This means that the Update() and other functions retain previous vector storage allocations, just resizing these vectors to zero when a reconstruction is performed, to avoid costly memory allocations\&. To delete both elements and the internal storage of the vectors, delete and create a new \fBNimbleRegion\fP object\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
\fBNimbleRegion\fP does not have a name or properties of its own and it is not managed by the \fBRegionInterface\fP, create it using its constructor and manage it with DES or any other parallel algorithm\&.

.PP
Grow(), Shrink() and ChangeShape() operations rely on the connectivity between equidimensional elements and nodes\&.

.PP
Thus far, Nimbleregion only works with linear elements\&.
.RE
.PP
Design specifications in detail: \fBNimbleRegion\fP for use in PDE_Integrators?

.PP
.IP "0." 4
Must be a template with integral parameter uint32_t dim
.IP "1." 4
Be a suitable plugin into the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP, meaning that it has the methods:

.PP
1\&.1 Must have a contructor that accepts iterators to node pointers 1\&.2 Should be able to change shape at low computational cost 1\&.3 Have the interfaces needed by the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP to function:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Must be based on vectors,
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Know its perimeter nodes / have nodes sorted into interior and perimeter ranges so that boundary conditions can be applied\&.
.PP

.IP "2." 4
\fBInterFace\fP / task share with DES algorithm to convey update information\&. 
.PP

